# Code owners for this repository.
#
# GitHub uses this file together with the "Require review from Code Owners"
# branch-protection rule on `main` to decide who must approve a pull request
# before it can merge (including via auto-merge).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# docs/** -> GitHub Copilot code review
#
# Rationale:
#   The Docs Auto-Merge workflow (.github/workflows/docs-auto-merge.yml) can
#   arm GitHub's native auto-merge on a PR when (a) every changed path is
#   under `docs/` and (b) the PR carries the `docs-only` label. Auto-merge
#   still respects branch protection, so making Copilot the sole code owner
#   of `docs/**` means a docs-only PR can only merge after Copilot code
#   review has submitted an APPROVED review. That gives the automated path a
#   real, model-based approval gate instead of merging with zero reviews.
#
# Prerequisite (out-of-band repo config, not versionable here):
#   * Branch protection on `main` must have
#     "Require a pull request before merging" ->
#     "Require review from Code Owners" enabled.
#     Without that rule this file has no effect.
#
# Non-docs paths (source, tests, workflows, config, .github/**, etc.) are
# intentionally left without an owner here so the normal human-review path
# stays the default for everything outside `docs/`.
/docs/**  @Copilot
